window.bookSummaryJSON = "<p><b>A runaway bride. A grumpy six-hundred-year-old vampire pretending to be human. A disaster waiting to happen.</b></p> <p>What could possibly be the most infuriating thing to a vampire disgusted by the internet? A twenty-six-year-old social media influencer who just ran out on her cheating ex-fiancé and insists on staying in Vlad's quiet castle.</p> <p>But he needs money to repair his ancestral home, and Aubrey needs a place to lick her wounds after getting her heart broken.</p> <p>He is ready to have humans invading his space. He is not, however, ready for her.</p> <p>She wants to feed him garlic, parades around in tiny shorts, and incenses him at every turn. Can he really play house with a human? Especially one he just can't seem to fight the urge to stay away from?</p> <p>The Holiday <i>meets</i> Dark Shadows <i>in this grumpy sunshine, spicy, paranormal romance. It is a full-length romance with a happily ever after. For mature listeners.</i></p>"; 
